 "findings": [
  {
   "sev": "info",
   "sevLabel": "Layout family",
   "title": "Transliteration (ITRANS-style)",
   "body": "<p>No positional keys to memorise — you spell Kannada (or ITRANS) in Roman letters and the engine composes the script. Byte-for-byte the Wikimedia jQuery.IME <code>kn-transliteration</code> rule set (M G Harish, HP Nadig).</p><p>Vowels are context-aware: a capital vowel key gives the independent form (A→ಆ, D→ಅ) — and its lowercase version after a consonant gives the vowel sign.</p>"
  },
  {
   "sev": "ok",
   "sevLabel": "Coverage",
   "title": "Full consonant + historic coverage by spelling",
   "body": "<p>All 34 consonants plus historic letters (ಱ via q/~r, ಞ via ~j/~n) are reachable. Long vowels by doubling the matra (i+i→ೀ, u+u→ೂ). Digit-7 <code>&amp;</code> ampersand and joiner escapes (x/X) are part of the ITRANS control set.</p>"
  }
 ],
